    values:originalText "(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply if the person acquired the goods, or held himself or herself out as acquiring the goods:  (a) for the purpose of re-supply; or  (b) for the purpose of using them up or transforming them, in trade or commerce:  (i) in the course of a process of production or manufacture; or  (ii) in the course of repairing or treating other goods or fixtures on land. Acquiring services as a consumer" ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply if the person acquired the goods, or held himself or herself out as acquiring the goods:  (a) for the purpose of re-supply; or  (b) for the purpose of using them up or transforming them, in trade or commerce:  (i) in the course of a process of production or manufacture; or  (ii) in the course of repairing or treating other goods or fixtures on land. Acquiring services as a consumer"@en ;
