concept:act-sch-2-sec-9-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9 Meaning of safety defect in relation to goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-9-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, goods have a safety defect if their safety is not such as persons generally are entitled to expect.  (2) In determining the extent of the safety of goods, regard is to be given to all relevant circumstances, including:  (a) the manner in which, and the purposes for which, they have been marketed; and  (b) their packaging; and  (c) the use of any mark in relation to them; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, goods have a safety defect if their safety is not such as persons generally are entitled to expect.  (2) In determining the extent of the safety of goods, regard is to be given to all relevant circumstances, including:  (a) the manner in which, and the purposes for which, they have been marketed; and  (b) their packaging; and  (c) the use of any mark in relation to them; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4809540c3010e6c435afceb16eff0077bea08c50f133c302c0750d2213f6d1d5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-9-2-ss-1 ;
