 was consistent with the supplier’s conduct in similar transactions between the supplier and other like business consumers; and  (g) the requirements of any applicable industry code; and  (h) the requirements of any other industry code, if the business consumer acted on the reasonable belief that the supplier would comply with that code; and  (i) the extent to which the supplier unreasonably failed to disclose to the business consumer:  (i) any intended conduct of the supplier that might affect the interests of the business consumer; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer .

