    values:originalText "(5) For the purpose of determining whether a person has contravened subsection (1):  (a) the court must not have regard to any circumstances that were not reasonably foreseeable at the time of the alleged contravention; and  (b) the court may have regard to circumstances existing before the commencement of this section but not to conduct engaged in before that commencement." ;
    skos:definition "(5) For the purpose of determining whether a person has contravened subsection (1):  (a) the court must not have regard to any circumstances that were not reasonably foreseeable at the time of the alleged contravention; and  (b) the court may have regard to circumstances existing before the commencement of this section but not to conduct engaged in before that commencement."@en ;
