concept:act-sch-2-sec-23-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23 Unfair terms of consumer contracts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A term of a consumer contract is void if:  (a) the term is unfair; and  (b) the contract is a standard form contract.  (2) The contract continues to bind the parties if it is capable of operating without the unfair term.  (3) A consumer contract is a contract for:  (a) a supply of goods or services; or  (b) a sale or grant of an interest in land; to an individual whose acquisition of the goods, services or interest is wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic or household use or consumption." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A term of a consumer contract is void if:  (a) the term is unfair; and  (b) the contract is a standard form contract.  (2) The contract continues to bind the parties if it is capable of operating without the unfair term.  (3) A consumer contract is a contract for:  (a) a supply of goods or services; or  (b) a sale or grant of an interest in land; to an individual whose acquisition of the goods, services or interest is wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic or household use or consumption."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d2da1e2fbf863e3f6c48f1673b680f56364e89b0dc1535f463ec334e763373fb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-23-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-23-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-23-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
