concept:act-sch-2-sec-64-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-64-2 ;
    values:originalText "(b) a similar article intended for use in obtaining cash, goods or services on credit;  (c) an article of a kind that persons carrying on business commonly issue to their customers, or prospective customers, for use in obtaining goods or services from those persons on credit; and includes an article that may be used as an article referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c).  (6) A debit card is:  (a) an article intended for use by a person in obtaining access to an account that is held by the person for the purpose of withdrawing or depositing cash or obtaining goods or services; or  (b) an article that may be used as an article referred to in paragraph (a)." ;
    skos:definition "(b) a similar article intended for use in obtaining cash, goods or services on credit;  (c) an article of a kind that persons carrying on business commonly issue to their customers, or prospective customers, for use in obtaining goods or services from those persons on credit; and includes an article that may be used as an article referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c).  (6) A debit card is:  (a) an article intended for use by a person in obtaining access to an account that is held by the person for the purpose of withdrawing or depositing cash or obtaining goods or services; or  (b) an article that may be used as an article referred to in paragraph (a)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "536f1379cf4b74cf41c0af79c67ac18f58812782dd9d1a2d3dc9831abba5322d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Prohibition on using certain articles for obtaining credit" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
