concept:act-sch-2-sec-50-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 Harassment and coercion"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-50-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not use physical force, or undue harassment or coercion, in connection with:  (a) the supply or possible supply of goods or services; or  (b) the payment for goods or services; or  (c) the sale or grant, or the possible sale or grant, of an interest in land; or  (d) the payment for an interest in land. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) Subsections (1)(c) and (d) do not affect the application of any other provision of Part 2-1 or this Part in relation to the supply or acquisition, or the possible supply or acquisition, of interests in land. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not use physical force, or undue harassment or coercion, in connection with:  (a) the supply or possible supply of goods or services; or  (b) the payment for goods or services; or  (c) the sale or grant, or the possible sale or grant, of an interest in land; or  (d) the payment for an interest in land. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) Subsections (1)(c) and (d) do not affect the application of any other provision of Part 2-1 or this Part in relation to the supply or acquisition, or the possible supply or acquisition, of interests in land. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a2eb32e0dae54a993f83d76b9007c9f7152cdd096d6cc303d0c4b04578753d43" ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-50-3-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-50-3-ss-2 ;
