doc:sch-2-sec-78-2-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "78(2) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A supplier does not fail to comply with the guarantee only because of the existence of a floating charge over the supplier’s assets unless and until the charge becomes fixed and enforceable by the person to whom the charge is given. Note: Section 339 of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 affects the meaning of the references in this subsection to a floating charge and a fixed charge." ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-78-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "78(3) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-78-2-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) a person (the supplier) supplies goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply is a supply of limited title; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 there is a guarantee that all securities, charges or encumbrances known to the supplier, and not known to the consumer, were disclosed to the consumer before the consumer agreed to the supply." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If:  (a) a person (the supplier) supplies goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply is a supply of limited title; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 there is a guarantee that all securities, charges or encumbrances known to the supplier, and not known to the consumer, were disclosed to the consumer before the consumer agreed to the supply."@en ;
