concept:act-sch-2-sec-54-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54 Guarantee as to acceptable quality"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-54-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the goods are of acceptable quality.  (2) Goods are of acceptable quality if they are as:  (a) fit for all the purposes for which goods of that kind are commonly supplied; and  (b) acceptable in appearance and finish; and  (c) free from defects; and  (d) safe; and  (e) durable; as a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the state and condition of the goods (including any hidden defects of the goods), would regard as acceptable having regard to the matters in subsection (3).  (3) The matters for the purposes of subsection (2) are:  (a) the nature of the goods; and  (b) the price of the goods (if relevant); and  (c) any statements made about the goods on any packaging or label on the goods; and  (d) any representation made about the goods by the supplier or manufacturer of the goods; and  (e) any other relevant circumstances relating to the supply of the goods. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the goods are of acceptable quality.  (2) Goods are of acceptable quality if they are as:  (a) fit for all the purposes for which goods of that kind are commonly supplied; and  (b) acceptable in appearance and finish; and  (c) free from defects; and  (d) safe; and  (e) durable; as a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the state and condition of the goods (including any hidden defects of the goods), would regard as acceptable having regard to the matters in subsection (3).  (3) The matters for the purposes of subsection (2) are:  (a) the nature of the goods; and  (b) the price of the goods (if relevant); and  (c) any statements made about the goods on any packaging or label on the goods; and  (d) any representation made about the goods by the supplier or manufacturer of the goods; and  (e) any other relevant circumstances relating to the supply of the goods. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "31f8bf731e699f56c73a469794fe7711a864f0eb86054557d47355e9db8c9fc8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "85"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-54-3-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-54-3-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-54-3-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.85" .
