d that:  (a) the consumer makes known, expressly or by implication, to:  (i) the supplier; or  (ii) a person by whom any prior negotiations or arrangements in relation to the acquisition of the goods were conducted or made; or  (b) the consumer makes known to the manufacturer of the goods either directly or through the supplier or the person referred to in paragraph (a)(ii).  (3) This section does not apply if the circumstances show that the consumer did not rely on, or that it was unreasonable for the consumer to rely on, the skill or judgment of the supplier, the person referred to in subsection (2)(a)(ii) or the manufacturer, as the case may be." ;
