    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-80-2-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "80(1) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person (the supplier) supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the goods are reasonably fit for any disclosed purpose, and for any purpose for which the supplier represents that they are reasonably fit. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    cof:pageNumber "86"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-80-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80(2) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-80-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A disclosed purpose is a particular purpose (whether or not that purpose is a purpose for which the goods are commonly supplied) for which the goods are being acquired by the consumer and that:  (a) the consumer makes known, expressly or by implication, to:  (i) the supplier; or  (ii) a person by whom any prior negotiations or arrangements in relation to the acquisition of the goods were conducted or made; or  (b) the consumer makes known to the manufacturer of the goods either directly or through the supplier or the person referred to in paragraph (a)(ii)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A disclosed purpose is a particular purpose (whether or not that purpose is a purpose for which the goods are commonly supplied) for which the goods are being acquired by the consumer and that:  (a) the consumer makes known, expressly or by implication, to:  (i) the supplier; or  (ii) a person by whom any prior negotiations or arrangements in relation to the acquisition of the goods were conducted or made; or  (b) the consumer makes known to the manufacturer of the goods either directly or through the supplier or the person referred to in paragraph (a)(ii)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ca4938e1c01e69eef9bc6dd09b0e619c20ca3454227911075dfa47226a230159" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-80-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "86"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of purpose for which goods are being acquired by consumer." ;
    dc:description "Express or implied knowledge to supplier, manufacturer, or person conducting prior negotiations." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
