    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "there is a guarantee that:  (c) the goods correspond with the sample or demonstration model in quality, state or condition; and  (d) if the goods are supplied by reference to a sample—the consumer will have a reasonable opportunity to compare the goods with the sample; and  (e) the goods are free from any defect that:  (i) would not be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample or demonstration model; and  (ii) would cause the goods not to be of acceptable quality.  (2) If goods are supplied by reference to a sample or demonstration model as well as by description, the guarantees in section 56 and in this section both apply." ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-58-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58 Guarantee as to repairs and spare parts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-58-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the manufacturer of the goods will take reasonable action to ensure that facilities for the repair of the goods, and parts for the goods, are reasonably available for a reasonable period after the goods are supplied.  (2) This section does not apply if the manufacturer took reasonable action to ensure that the consumer would be given written notice, at or before the time when the consumer agrees to the supply of the goods, that:  (a) facilities for the repair of the goods would not be available or would not be available after a specified period; or  (b) parts for the goods would not be available or would not be available after a specified period." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the manufacturer of the goods will take reasonable action to ensure that facilities for the repair of the goods, and parts for the goods, are reasonably available for a reasonable period after the goods are supplied.  (2) This section does not apply if the manufacturer took reasonable action to ensure that the consumer would be given written notice, at or before the time when the consumer agrees to the supply of the goods, that:  (a) facilities for the repair of the goods would not be available or would not be available after a specified period; or  (b) parts for the goods would not be available or would not be available after a specified period."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eac398e558b564ac929367f6f7ba3f37331dbdfc01dcc3ade8c2acfb00aaf78a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
