concept:act-sch-2-sec-59-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59 Guarantee as to express warranties"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-59-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the manufacturer of the goods will comply with any express warranty given or made by the manufacturer in relation to the goods.  (2) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the supplier will comply with any express warranty given or made by the supplier in relation to the goods. Subdivision B—Guarantees relating to the supply of services" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the manufacturer of the goods will comply with any express warranty given or made by the manufacturer in relation to the goods.  (2) If:  (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and  (b) the supply does not occur by way of sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the supplier will comply with any express warranty given or made by the supplier in relation to the goods. Subdivision B—Guarantees relating to the supply of services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2c0380d4e703c47419f585e4a54a6f42a6791919811696029f9f7b551afcb973" ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
