concept:act-sch-2-sec-84-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "84 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-84-2 ;
    values:originalText "there is a guarantee that the services, and any product resulting from the services, will be of such a nature, and quality, state or condition, that they might reasonably be expected to achieve that result.  (3) This section does not apply if the circumstances show that the consumer did not rely on, or that it was unreasonable for the consumer to rely on, the skill or judgment of the supplier.  (4) This section does not apply to a supply of services of a professional nature by a qualified architect or engineer." ;
    skos:definition "there is a guarantee that the services, and any product resulting from the services, will be of such a nature, and quality, state or condition, that they might reasonably be expected to achieve that result.  (3) This section does not apply if the circumstances show that the consumer did not rely on, or that it was unreasonable for the consumer to rely on, the skill or judgment of the supplier.  (4) This section does not apply to a supply of services of a professional nature by a qualified architect or engineer."@en ;
