concept:act-sch-2-sec-90-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "90 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-90-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An invitation merely to quote a price for a supply is not taken, for the purposes of subsection (1)(c), to be an invitation to enter into negotiations for a supply.  (3) An agreement is also an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are unsolicited consumer agreements.  (4) However, despite subsections (1) and (3), an agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are not unsolicited consumer agreements." ;
    skos:definition "(2) An invitation merely to quote a price for a supply is not taken, for the purposes of subsection (1)(c), to be an invitation to enter into negotiations for a supply.  (3) An agreement is also an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are unsolicited consumer agreements.  (4) However, despite subsections (1) and (3), an agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are not unsolicited consumer agreements."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "459c396be5ac2603036142c80b5c68932f97e3f3be2faf9bdf5c2b5a23c22ebd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-90-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-90-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-90-2-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.96" .
doc:sch-2-sec-90-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "90 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An invitation merely to quote a price for a supply is not taken, for the purposes of subsection (1)(c), to be an invitation to enter into negotiations for a supply.  (3) An agreement is also an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are unsolicited consumer agreements.  (4) However, despite subsections (1) and (3), an agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are not unsolicited consumer agreements." ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

