doc:sch-2-sec-90-2-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "90(4) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) However, despite subsections (1) and (3), an agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement if it is an agreement of a kind that the regulations provide are not unsolicited consumer agreements." ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-70-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "70 Presumption that agreements are unsolicited consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-70-3 ;
    values:originalText "agreements  (1) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), an agreement is presumed to be an unsolicited consumer agreement if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the agreement is an unsolicited consumer agreement; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement.  (2) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), it is presumed that a proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the proposed agreement would not be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made." ;
    skos:definition "agreements  (1) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), an agreement is presumed to be an unsolicited consumer agreement if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the agreement is an unsolicited consumer agreement; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the agreement is not an unsolicited consumer agreement.  (2) In a proceeding relating to a contravention or possible contravention of this Division (other than a criminal proceeding), it is presumed that a proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made if:  (a) a party to the proceeding alleges that the proposed agreement would be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made; and  (b) no other party to the proceeding proves that the proposed agreement would not be an unsolicited consumer agreement if it were made."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bbf2df780dbc780dcd702a1bb88cde7d6f686789b6249d88ad67e102a6d185f6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-70-3-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-70-3-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
