concept:act-sch-2-sec-84-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "84 Obligations of suppliers on termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-84-3 ;
    values:originalText "If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the supplier under the agreement must, ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 immediately upon being notified of the termination, return or refund to the consumer under the agreement any consideration (or the value of any consideration) that the consumer gave under the agreement or a related contract or instrument. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this section." ;
    skos:definition "If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the supplier under the agreement must, ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 immediately upon being notified of the termination, return or refund to the consumer under the agreement any consideration (or the value of any consideration) that the consumer gave under the agreement or a related contract or instrument. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dac2483d28be95768de845565835db45257bb69af8ec9101deefc9ce425477e8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Supplier must return consideration to consumer upon termination of unsolicited consumer agreement." ;
    dc:description "Return or refund" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
