doc:sch-2-sec-84-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "84 Obligations of suppliers on termination" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the supplier under the agreement must, ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 immediately upon being notified of the termination, return or refund to the consumer under the agreement any consideration (or the value of any consideration) that the consumer gave under the agreement or a related contract or instrument. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-85-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85 Obligations and rights of consumers on termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-85-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the consumer under the agreement must, within a reasonable time:  (a) return to the supplier under the agreement any goods:  (i) that have been received from the supplier under the agreement; and  (ii) that the consumer has not already consumed; or  (b) notify the supplier of the place where the supplier may collect the goods.  (2) The goods become the property of the consumer, freed and discharged from all liens and charges of any description, if:  (a) the consumer gives notice to the supplier under subsection (1)(b); and  (b) the supplier does not collect the goods within 30 days after the termination of the contract.  (3) If:  (a) the agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82 after the end of the period of 10 business days starting:  (i) if the agreement was not negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the agreement was made; or  (ii) if the agreement was negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the consumer was given the agreement document relating to the agreement; and  (b) the consumer returns the goods to the supplier, or the supplier collects the goods, under this section; and  (c) the consumer has failed to take reasonable care of the goods; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82, the consumer under the agreement must, within a reasonable time:  (a) return to the supplier under the agreement any goods:  (i) that have been received from the supplier under the agreement; and  (ii) that the consumer has not already consumed; or  (b) notify the supplier of the place where the supplier may collect the goods.  (2) The goods become the property of the consumer, freed and discharged from all liens and charges of any description, if:  (a) the consumer gives notice to the supplier under subsection (1)(b); and  (b) the supplier does not collect the goods within 30 days after the termination of the contract.  (3) If:  (a) the agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82 after the end of the period of 10 business days starting:  (i) if the agreement was not negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the agreement was made; or  (ii) if the agreement was negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the consumer was given the agreement document relating to the agreement; and  (b) the consumer returns the goods to the supplier, or the supplier collects the goods, under this section; and  (c) the consumer has failed to take reasonable care of the goods; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "67745f3da64bd44bd130e307cc1ae5d1c2d96e6130b6eb9612b481a4aced6554" ;
    cof:pageNumber "105"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-85-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-85-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-85-2-ss-3 ;
