concept:act-sch-2-sec-100 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "100 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-100 ;
    values:originalText "the consumer is liable to pay compensation to the supplier for the damage to, or depreciation in the value of, the goods.  (4) The compensation is recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction.  (5) However, the consumer is not liable for any such damage or depreciation attributable to normal use of the goods or to circumstances beyond the consumer’s control.  (6) If:  (a) an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82 after the end of the period of 10 business days starting:  (i) if the agreement was not negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the agreement was made; or  (ii) if the agreement was negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the consumer was given the agreement document relating to the agreement; and  (b) prior to the termination, but after the end of that period, a service was supplied under the agreement; the termination does not affect any liability of the consumer under the agreement to provide consideration for the service." ;
    skos:definition "the consumer is liable to pay compensation to the supplier for the damage to, or depreciation in the value of, the goods.  (4) The compensation is recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction.  (5) However, the consumer is not liable for any such damage or depreciation attributable to normal use of the goods or to circumstances beyond the consumer’s control.  (6) If:  (a) an unsolicited consumer agreement is terminated in accordance with section 82 after the end of the period of 10 business days starting:  (i) if the agreement was not negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the agreement was made; or  (ii) if the agreement was negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the consumer was given the agreement document relating to the agreement; and  (b) prior to the termination, but after the end of that period, a service was supplied under the agreement; the termination does not affect any liability of the consumer under the agreement to provide consideration for the service."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ebdd93df8fdbd268adcc6a5aefa2cd5b9a3e24b595cbfc9d6f7d5a83774ec379" ;
    cof:pageNumber "106"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-100-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-100-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-100-ss-6 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
