concept:act-sch-2-sec-97-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "97 Termination of lay-by agreements by consumers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-97-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A consumer who is party to a lay-by agreement may terminate the agreement at any time before the consumer goods to which the agreement relates are delivered to the consumer under the agreement.  (2) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that the agreement does not require the consumer to pay a charge (a termination charge) for the termination of the agreement unless: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A consumer who is party to a lay-by agreement may terminate the agreement at any time before the consumer goods to which the agreement relates are delivered to the consumer under the agreement.  (2) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that the agreement does not require the consumer to pay a charge (a termination charge) for the termination of the agreement unless: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "db7056a1feb0d2e7e90c4aba56c1502d80cc7c3f4f62ba040756f848dd4266c3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-97-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-97-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.111" .
