doc:sch-2-sec-97-2-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "97(2) Termination of lay-by agreements by consumers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that the agreement does not require the consumer to pay a charge (a termination charge) for the termination of the agreement unless: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-106-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-106-2 ;
    values:originalText "(a) the agreement is terminated by the consumer; and  (b) the supplier has not breached the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (3) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that, if the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable, the amount of the charge is not more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(a) the agreement is terminated by the consumer; and  (b) the supplier has not breached the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (3) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement must ensure that, if the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable, the amount of the charge is not more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ccdaa7e1343ca17cd2d0242560eb6d533b08efa35fbca220772525e9a50abb37" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Supplier must ensure termination charge is reasonable." ;
