    skos:definition "(3) A safety standard for product related services of a particular kind may consist of such requirements about the following matters as are reasonably necessary to prevent or reduce risk of injury to any person:  (a) the manner in which services of that kind are supplied (including, but not limited to, the method of supply);  (b) the skills or qualifications of persons who supply such services;  (c) the materials used in supplying such services;  (d) the testing of such services; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (e) the form and content of warnings, instructions or other information about such services."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "28c047d5d980d1931738051865ec6cb6031a90416f0ab33815b29c25da519ef4" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-104-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Safety standards for product-related services may require specific requirements to prevent or reduce risk of injury." ;
