concept:act-sch-2-sec-106-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106 Supplying etc. consumer goods that do not comply with safety"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-106-3 ;
    values:originalText "standards  (1) A person must not, in trade or commerce, supply consumer goods of a particular kind if:  (a) a safety standard for consumer goods of that kind is in force; and  (b) those goods do not comply with the standard. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) A person must not, in trade or commerce, offer for supply (other than for export) consumer goods the supply of which is prohibited by subsection (1). Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "standards  (1) A person must not, in trade or commerce, supply consumer goods of a particular kind if:  (a) a safety standard for consumer goods of that kind is in force; and  (b) those goods do not comply with the standard. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection.  (2) A person must not, in trade or commerce, offer for supply (other than for export) consumer goods the supply of which is prohibited by subsection (1). Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0b21aaddae93d0233f598f4d15c6bdc695206094e89cba27044e721a83c79219" ;
