concept:act-sch-2-sec-112-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "112 Interaction of multiple interim bans"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-112-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) an interim ban (the original ban) on consumer goods of a particular kind (the banned goods) is imposed by a responsible Minister other than the Commonwealth Minister; and  (b) while the original ban is in force, the Commonwealth Minister imposes an interim ban (the Commonwealth ban):  (i) on the banned goods; or  (ii) on consumer goods of a kind that includes the banned goods; the original ban, to the extent that it is a ban on the banned goods, ceases to be in force immediately before the Commonwealth ban comes into force.  (2) If:  (a) an interim ban (the original ban) on product related services of a particular kind (the banned services) is imposed by a responsible Minister other than the Commonwealth Minister; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) an interim ban (the original ban) on consumer goods of a particular kind (the banned goods) is imposed by a responsible Minister other than the Commonwealth Minister; and  (b) while the original ban is in force, the Commonwealth Minister imposes an interim ban (the Commonwealth ban):  (i) on the banned goods; or  (ii) on consumer goods of a kind that includes the banned goods; the original ban, to the extent that it is a ban on the banned goods, ceases to be in force immediately before the Commonwealth ban comes into force.  (2) If:  (a) an interim ban (the original ban) on product related services of a particular kind (the banned services) is imposed by a responsible Minister other than the Commonwealth Minister; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
