concept:act-sch-2-sec-121-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "121 Temporary exemption under the Mutual Recognition Act 1992"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-121-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind is in force; and  (b) the interim ban was not imposed by the Commonwealth Minister; the goods are taken, for the purposes of section 15 of the Mutual Recognition Act 1992, to be goods of a kind that are declared, in the manner provided by section 15(1) of that Act, to be goods to which that section applies.  (2) This section does not affect the application of section 15(3) of that Act in relation to such an exemption. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind is in force; and  (b) the interim ban was not imposed by the Commonwealth Minister; the goods are taken, for the purposes of section 15 of the Mutual Recognition Act 1992, to be goods of a kind that are declared, in the manner provided by section 15(1) of that Act, to be goods to which that section applies.  (2) This section does not affect the application of section 15(3) of that Act in relation to such an exemption. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "124590966142b8a1db16137627c60494dbd9c65869f166ba750b94fcf5899786" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-121-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-121-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
