concept:act-sch-2-sec-128-3-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "128(6) Notification requirements for a voluntary recall of consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-128-3-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) A person who is required to give a notice under subsection (4) must, within 10 days after giving the notice, give a copy of the notice to the Commonwealth Minister. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(6) A person who is required to give a notice under subsection (4) must, within 10 days after giving the notice, give a copy of the notice to the Commonwealth Minister. Note: A pecuniary penalty may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e8709673c1d9e69f831250d9a4201b6b786c5e281cc2b246535b9ddf5bab10d6" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-128-3 ;
