concept:act-sch-2-sec-141-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "141 Liability for loss or damage suffered by a person if land,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-141-2 ;
    values:originalText "buildings or fixtures are destroyed or damaged  (1) A manufacturer of goods is liable to compensate a person if:  (a) the manufacturer supplies the goods in trade or commerce; and  (b) the goods have a safety defect; and  (c) land, buildings or fixtures are destroyed or damaged because of the safety defect; and  (d) the land, buildings or fixtures are ordinarily acquired for private use; and  (e) the person used, or intended to use, the land, buildings or fixtures for private use; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "buildings or fixtures are destroyed or damaged  (1) A manufacturer of goods is liable to compensate a person if:  (a) the manufacturer supplies the goods in trade or commerce; and  (b) the goods have a safety defect; and  (c) land, buildings or fixtures are destroyed or damaged because of the safety defect; and  (d) the land, buildings or fixtures are ordinarily acquired for private use; and  (e) the person used, or intended to use, the land, buildings or fixtures for private use; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
