concept:act-sch-2-sec-153-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "153 Misleading conduct relating to employment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-153-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in relation to employment that is to be, or may be, offered by the person or by another person, engages in conduct that is liable to mislead persons seeking the employment as to:  (a) the availability, nature, terms or conditions of the employment; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in relation to employment that is to be, or may be, offered by the person or by another person, engages in conduct that is liable to mislead persons seeking the employment as to:  (a) the availability, nature, terms or conditions of the employment; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "055a7d053e07e816c57314bde447ba23c53c1477d5b2d78915aa5e27fcbde3d4" ;
