concept:act-sch-2-sec-158-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "158 Wrongly accepting payment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-158-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, accepts payment or other consideration for goods or services; and  (b) at the time of the acceptance, the person intends not to supply the goods or services. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.  (2) Strict liability applies to subsection (1)(a).  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, accepts payment or other consideration for goods or services; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, accepts payment or other consideration for goods or services; and  (b) at the time of the acceptance, the person intends not to supply the goods or services. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.  (2) Strict liability applies to subsection (1)(a).  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, accepts payment or other consideration for goods or services; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "960e0bfd4b7bef302dc80f0f66bf30176da9771baf30fed975fc508da39c9b12" ;
    cof:pageNumber "161"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-158-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-158-2-ss-2 ;
