doc:sch-2-sec-156-3-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "156(7) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, accepts payment or other consideration for goods or services; and  (b) the person fails to supply all the goods or services:  (i) within the period specified by or on behalf of the person at or before the time the payment or other consideration was accepted; or  (ii) if no period is specified at or before that time—within a reasonable time. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000." ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-156-3-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "156(8) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-156-3-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) Subsection (7) does not apply if:  (a) the person’s failure to supply all the goods or services within the period, or within a reasonable time, was due to the act or omission of another person, or to some other cause beyond the person’s control; and  (b) the person took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the failure." ;
    skos:definition "(8) Subsection (7) does not apply if:  (a) the person’s failure to supply all the goods or services within the period, or within a reasonable time, was due to the act or omission of another person, or to some other cause beyond the person’s control; and  (b) the person took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the failure."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "30816ac92fa6b23229ef8e7a03cfde3101a6c9d0e4d59aa0b1cde6d7a9672e98" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-156-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Due diligence required to avoid failure in supplying goods or services." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.162" ;
    cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-156-3-ss-8-norm .
