    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person sends a credit card or a debit card, or an article that may be used as a credit card and a debit card, to another person; and  (b) either:  (i) the person had issued the card; or  (ii) the card was sent on behalf of the person who had issued the card. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000."@en ;
