concept:act-sch-2-sec-164-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "164 Participation in pyramid schemes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-164-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if the person participates in a pyramid scheme. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.  (2) A person commits an offence if the person induces another person to participate in a pyramid scheme. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.  (3) Subsections (1) and (2) are offences of strict liability. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if the person participates in a pyramid scheme. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.  (2) A person commits an offence if the person induces another person to participate in a pyramid scheme. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.  (3) Subsections (1) and (2) are offences of strict liability. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "276d17971a799b547b0956130797ae2488b143a4b44ff160572956b9d3ecfe4b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
