concept:act-sch-2-sec-174-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "174 Requirement to give document to the consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-174-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The dealer who negotiated an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement was not negotiated by telephone; and  (b) the dealer does not give a copy of the agreement to the consumer under the agreement immediately after the consumer signs the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) The dealer who negotiated an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement was negotiated by telephone; and  (b) the dealer does not, within 5 business days after the agreement was made or such longer period agreed by the parties, give to the consumer under the agreement:  (i) personally; or  (ii) by post; or  (iii) with the consumer’s consent—by electronic communication;  an agreement document evidencing the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The dealer who negotiated an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement was not negotiated by telephone; and  (b) the dealer does not give a copy of the agreement to the consumer under the agreement immediately after the consumer signs the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) The dealer who negotiated an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement was negotiated by telephone; and  (b) the dealer does not, within 5 business days after the agreement was made or such longer period agreed by the parties, give to the consumer under the agreement:  (i) personally; or  (ii) by post; or  (iii) with the consumer’s consent—by electronic communication;  an agreement document evidencing the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cfb85f0c65279a45a3077b434fc0a08cef27afbef81e8b2b697fc3a6b732b560" ;
    cof:pageNumber "179"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-174-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-174-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.179" .
