concept:act-sch-2-sec-177-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "177 Requirements for amendments of unsolicited consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-177-2 ;
    values:originalText "agreements  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if any amendments to the agreement are not signed by both parties to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Subdivision C—Terminating unsolicited consumer agreements" ;
    skos:definition "agreements  (1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if any amendments to the agreement are not signed by both parties to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Subdivision C—Terminating unsolicited consumer agreements"@en ;
