concept:act-sch-2-sec-179-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179 Prohibition on supplies for 10 business days"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-179-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the supplier:  (i) supplies to the consumer under the agreement the goods or services to be supplied under the agreement; or  (ii) accepts any payment, or any other consideration, in connection with those goods or services; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (iii) requires any payment, or any other consideration, in connection with those goods or services; and  (b) the supply, acceptance or requirement occurs during the period of 10 business days starting:  (i) if the agreement was not negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the agreement was made; or  (ii) if the agreement was negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the consumer was given the agreement document relating to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Strict liability applies to subsection (1)(a)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the supplier:  (i) supplies to the consumer under the agreement the goods or services to be supplied under the agreement; or  (ii) accepts any payment, or any other consideration, in connection with those goods or services; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (iii) requires any payment, or any other consideration, in connection with those goods or services; and  (b) the supply, acceptance or requirement occurs during the period of 10 business days starting:  (i) if the agreement was not negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the agreement was made; or  (ii) if the agreement was negotiated by telephone—at the start of the first business day after the day on which the consumer was given the agreement document relating to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000.  (2) Strict liability applies to subsection (1)(a)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6226f23a23027aefb6d1fc21583f6caf8a4f8e01a39fd86fc7b2ef245b574dee" ;
    cof:pageNumber "182"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-179-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-179-2-ss-2 ;
