    cml:premiseText "The agreement includes or purports to include a provision that is void because of section 89(1)." ;
    cml:conclusionText "An offence is committed if the supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement includes such a provision." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-182-2-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "182(1) Certain provisions of unsolicited consumer agreements void" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if the agreement includes, or purports to include, a ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 provision (however described) that is, or would be, void because of section 89(1). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000." ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-182-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "182(2) Certain provisions of unsolicited consumer agreements void"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-182-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if the supplier attempts to enforce or rely on a provision (however described) that is void because of section 89(1). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The supplier under an unsolicited consumer agreement commits an offence if the supplier attempts to enforce or rely on a provision (however described) that is void because of section 89(1). Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$10,000."@en ;
