doc:sch-2-sec-187-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "187 Application of this Division to certain conduct covered by the" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Corporations Act  This Division does not apply in relation to conduct to which section 736, 992A or 992AA of the Corporations Act 2001 applies. Note: Section 736 of the Corporations Act 2001 prohibits hawking of securities. Section 992A of that Act prohibits hawking of certain financial products. Section 992AA of that Act prohibits hawking of managed investment products. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    cof:pageNumber "186"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-189-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "189 Termination charges"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-189-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if the agreement requires the consumer to pay a termination charge. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$6,000.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the termination charge is payable only if:  (a) the agreement is terminated by the consumer; and  (b) the supplier has not breached the agreement.  (3) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable; and  (b) the amount of the charge is more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if the agreement requires the consumer to pay a termination charge. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$6,000.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the termination charge is payable only if:  (a) the agreement is terminated by the consumer; and  (b) the supplier has not breached the agreement.  (3) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable; and  (b) the amount of the charge is more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6ed0b97b64946d5c195c1a18dfa2b7fbbf86ddae2fd76556a64efc517631d848" ;
    cof:pageNumber "187"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-189-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-189-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-189-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.187" .
