doc:sch-2-sec-189-2-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "189(3) Termination charges" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if:  (a) the agreement provides that a termination charge is payable; and  (b) the amount of the charge is more than the supplier’s reasonable costs in relation to the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    cof:pageNumber "187"^^xsd:integer .

