concept:act-sch-2-sec-190-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "190 Termination of lay-by agreements by suppliers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-190-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if the supplier terminates the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$6,000.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the consumer who is a party to the agreement breached a term of the agreement; or  (b) the supplier is no longer engaged in trade or commerce; or  (c) the consumer goods to which the agreement relates are no longer available.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A supplier of consumer goods who is a party to a lay-by agreement commits an offence if the supplier terminates the agreement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$30,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$6,000.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the consumer who is a party to the agreement breached a term of the agreement; or  (b) the supplier is no longer engaged in trade or commerce; or  (c) the consumer goods to which the agreement relates are no longer available.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fdef8f3ff2ffedae9af31ba11436ef340b5b329147194f428b4ec5f776a10a3c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
