concept:act-sch-2-sec-194-2-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "194(5) Supplying etc. consumer goods that do not comply with safety"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-194-2-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, exports consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) a safety standard for consumer goods of that kind is in force; and  (c) those goods do not comply with the standard. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000." ;
    skos:definition "(5) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, exports consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) a safety standard for consumer goods of that kind is in force; and  (c) those goods do not comply with the standard. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a721291af6bb434e288e6d48fd9428d3709e02018b53231d18e29875a68f3cfa" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-194-2 ;
