doc:sch-2-sec-199-2-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "199(2) Compliance with recall orders" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) a recall notice for consumer goods is in force; and  (b) the person, in trade or commerce:  (i) if the notice identifies a defect in, or a dangerous characteristic of, the consumer goods—supplies consumer goods of the kind to which the notice relates which contain that defect or have that characteristic; or  (ii) in any other case—supplies consumer goods of the kind to which the notice relates. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000." ;
    cof:pageNumber "195"^^xsd:integer .

