concept:act-sch-2-sec-200-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "200 Notification by persons who supply consumer goods outside"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-200-2 ;
    values:originalText "Australia if there is compulsory recall  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is required by section 125(4) to give a copy of a notice to a responsible Minister; and  (b) the person refuses or fails to give the copy as required by that section. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
