concept:act-sch-2-sec-204-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "204 Supplying etc. services that do not comply with information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-204-2 ;
    values:originalText "standards  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, supplies services of a particular kind; and  (b) an information standard for services of that kind is in force; and  (c) the person has not complied with the standard in relation to the services. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "standards  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, supplies services of a particular kind; and  (b) an information standard for services of that kind is in force; and  (c) the person has not complied with the standard in relation to the services. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e89c8ed38efa95fbec39e0e590c76462b43c66e08285a6bbe3d019783526924b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "199"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Supplying services that do not comply with information standards is an offence." ;
