concept:act-sch-2-sec-205-2-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "205(1) Compliance with substantiation notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-205-2-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in compliance or purported compliance with a substantiation notice given by the regulator:  (a) gives to the regulator false or misleading information; or  (b) produces to the regulator documents that contain false or misleading information. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$27,500; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$5,500. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if the person, in compliance or purported compliance with a substantiation notice given by the regulator:  (a) gives to the regulator false or misleading information; or  (b) produces to the regulator documents that contain false or misleading information. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$27,500; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$5,500. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2f445bbaa094aa549643dbae7338f3edf93f6de264eacdf2b148da20ea8e4c97" ;
