concept:act-sch-2-sec-196-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "196 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-196-3 ;
    values:originalText "(2) This section does not apply to:  (a) information that the person could not have known was false or misleading; or  (b) the production to the regulator of a document containing false or misleading information if the document is accompanied by a statement of the person that the information is false or misleading.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(2) This section does not apply to:  (a) information that the person could not have known was false or misleading; or  (b) the production to the regulator of a document containing false or misleading information if the document is accompanied by a statement of the person that the information is false or misleading.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ee6daa191d6943bb0935e00baf9b502bdc096d1cd69c33c8e7a5dcda7ad87939" ;
