doc:sch-2-sec-198-3-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "198(2) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the act or default of another person who was, at the time when the contravention occurred:  (a) an employee or agent of the defendant; or  (b) if the defendant is a body corporate—a director, employee or agent of the defendant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "204"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-198-3-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "198(3) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-198-3-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If a defence provided by subsection (1) involves an allegation that a contravention was due to the act or default of another person, the defendant is not entitled to rely on that defence unless:  (a) the court gives leave; or  (b) the defendant has, not later than 7 days before the day on which the hearing of the proceeding commences, served on the person who instituted the proceeding a written notice giving such information as the defendant then had that would identify or assist in identifying the other person." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If a defence provided by subsection (1) involves an allegation that a contravention was due to the act or default of another person, the defendant is not entitled to rely on that defence unless:  (a) the court gives leave; or  (b) the defendant has, not later than 7 days before the day on which the hearing of the proceeding commences, served on the person who instituted the proceeding a written notice giving such information as the defendant then had that would identify or assist in identifying the other person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1613e4c17055975201ef30efad281bcef70acb6b6ea2e9ffa67f58f8ab173d33" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-198-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "204"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defendant must provide notice to the person who instituted the proceeding before relying on a defence that involves an allegation of another person's act or default." ;
    dc:description "Notice" ;
