doc:sch-2-sec-210-3-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "210(3) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The pecuniary penalty payable under subsection (1) is not to exceed the amount worked out using the following table:  Amount of pecuniary penalty Item For each act or omission to which this section applies that relates to ... the pecuniary penalty is not to exceed ... a provision of Part 2-2 (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1.1 million; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $220,000. a provision of Part 3-1 (other than section 47(1)) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1.1 million; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $220,000. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 Amount of pecuniary penalty Item For each act or omission to which this section applies that relates to ... the pecuniary penalty is not to exceed ... section 47(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$5,000; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$1,000. section 66(2) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$50,000; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $10,000. a provision of Division 2 of" ;
    cof:pageNumber "216"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-212-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "212 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-212-3 ;
    values:originalText "Amount of pecuniary penalty Item For each act or omission to which this section applies that relates to ... the pecuniary penalty is not to exceed ... section 125(4) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$16,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$3,300. section 127(1) or (2) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1.1 million; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $220,000. section 128(2) or (6), 131(1) or 132(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$16,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$3,300. section 136(1), (2) or (3) or 137(1) or (2) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1.1 million; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $220,000. section 221(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$16,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$3,300. section 222(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$27,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$5,500.  (4) If conduct constitutes a contravention of 2 or more provisions referred to in subsection (1)(a):  (a) a proceeding may be instituted under this Schedule against a person in relation to the contravention of any one or more of the provisions; but  (b) a person is not liable to more than one pecuniary penalty under this section in respect of the same conduct. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "Amount of pecuniary penalty Item For each act or omission to which this section applies that relates to ... the pecuniary penalty is not to exceed ... section 125(4) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$16,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$3,300. section 127(1) or (2) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1.1 million; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $220,000. section 128(2) or (6), 131(1) or 132(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$16,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$3,300. section 136(1), (2) or (3) or 137(1) or (2) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1.1 million; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate— $220,000. section 221(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$16,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$3,300. section 222(1) (a) if the person is a body corporate—$27,500; or (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$5,500.  (4) If conduct constitutes a contravention of 2 or more provisions referred to in subsection (1)(a):  (a) a proceeding may be instituted under this Schedule against a person in relation to the contravention of any one or more of the provisions; but  (b) a person is not liable to more than one pecuniary penalty under this section in respect of the same conduct. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6a89d89be03c99fe8bc1a62ceca564212e0fa7dd006fa4cbac16929571828ac4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Pecuniary penalty limits for certain acts and omissions" ;
    dc:description "$16,500 or $3,300" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.218" ;
    cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-212-3-norm .
