doc:sch-2-sec-227-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "227 Preference must be given to compensation for victims" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If a court considers that:  (a) it is appropriate to order a person (the defendant) to pay a pecuniary penalty under section 224 in relation to:  (i) a contravention of a provision referred to in subsection (1)(a) of that section; or  (ii) conduct referred to in subsection (1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of that section that relates to a contravention such a provision; and  (b) it is appropriate to order the defendant to pay compensation to a person who has suffered loss or damage as result of that contravention or conduct; and  (c) the defendant does not have sufficient financial resources to pay both the pecuniary penalty and the compensation; the court must give preference to making an order for compensation." ;
    cof:pageNumber "220"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-228-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "228 Civil action for recovery of pecuniary penalties"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-228-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The regulator may institute a proceeding in a court for the recovery on behalf of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, as the case may be, of a pecuniary penalty referred to in section 224.  (2) A proceeding under subsection (1) may be commenced at any time within 6 years after the contravention or conduct. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The regulator may institute a proceeding in a court for the recovery on behalf of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, as the case may be, of a pecuniary penalty referred to in section 224.  (2) A proceeding under subsection (1) may be commenced at any time within 6 years after the contravention or conduct. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d3080572ecafae3246f2304a3fa080b3c3fb965c4f3774f63e62cb626a672f2f" ;
