doc:sch-2-sec-232-2-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "232(3) Injunctions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (1) applies in relation to conduct constituted by applying or relying on, or purporting to apply or rely on, a term of a consumer contract that has been declared under section 250 to be an unfair term as if the conduct were a contravention of a provision of Chapter 2." ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-232-2-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "232(4) Injunctions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-232-2-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The power of the court to grant an injunction under subsection (1) restraining a person from engaging in conduct may be exercised:  (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of a kind referred to in that subsection; and  (b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct of that kind; and  (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person engages in conduct of that kind. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(4) The power of the court to grant an injunction under subsection (1) restraining a person from engaging in conduct may be exercised:  (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of a kind referred to in that subsection; and  (b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct of that kind; and  (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person engages in conduct of that kind. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c5ac2283af6deade2a1e7361311a15ca555f1677c8e1f1e6dd5da8b42ee3b12b" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-232-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court power to grant injunction under subsection (1) can be exercised regardless of intent or previous conduct." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.222" ;
