doc:sch-2-sec-232-2-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "232(4) Injunctions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The power of the court to grant an injunction under subsection (1) restraining a person from engaging in conduct may be exercised:  (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of a kind referred to in that subsection; and  (b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct of that kind; and  (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person engages in conduct of that kind. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-232-2-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "232(5) Injunctions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-232-2-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Without limiting subsection (1), the court may grant an injunction under that subsection restraining a person from carrying on a business or supplying goods or services (whether or not as part of, or incidental to, the carrying on of another business):  (a) for a specified period; or  (b) except on specified terms and conditions." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Without limiting subsection (1), the court may grant an injunction under that subsection restraining a person from carrying on a business or supplying goods or services (whether or not as part of, or incidental to, the carrying on of another business):  (a) for a specified period; or  (b) except on specified terms and conditions."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6a9e6fedf7b26e9a854ca7a02c8199a03c81b167b7e88353c9ab37be2aac13bb" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-232-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Restraining a person from carrying on a business or supplying goods or services" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
