concept:act-sch-2-sec-250-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "250 Declarations relating to consumer contracts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-250-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A court may, on the application of a party to a consumer contract or on the application of the regulator, declare that a term of such a contract is an unfair term.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply unless the consumer contract is a standard form contract.  (3) Subsection (1) does not limit any other power of the court to make declarations. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A court may, on the application of a party to a consumer contract or on the application of the regulator, declare that a term of such a contract is an unfair term.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply unless the consumer contract is a standard form contract.  (3) Subsection (1) does not limit any other power of the court to make declarations. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "07a41bbd8e44589a530191b1eb257a853c6c00efb292745df41350203d1bf28b" ;
