    skos:prefLabel "256 Cost of producing or manufacturing goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-256-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The cost of producing or manufacturing goods is worked out, for the purposes of section 255, by adding up the following amounts:  (a) the amount of expenditure on materials in respect of the goods;  (b) the amount of expenditure on labour in respect of the goods;  (c) the amount of expenditure on overheads in respect of the goods; each worked out in accordance with this table:  Cost of producing or manufacturing goods Item This amount of expenditure: is worked out as follows: Expenditure on materials in respect of the goods The cost of materials used in the production or manufacture of the goods: (a) that is incurred by the manufacturer of the goods; and (b) that has not been prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2)(a). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 Cost of producing or manufacturing goods Item This amount of expenditure: is worked out as follows: Expenditure on labour in respect of the goods The sum of each labour cost: (a) that is incurred by the manufacturer of the goods; and (b) that relates to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (c) that can reasonably be allocated to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (d) that has not been prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2)(b). Expenditure on overheads in respect of the goods The sum of each overhead cost: (a) that is incurred by the manufacturer of the goods; and (b) that relates to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (c) that can reasonably be allocated to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (d) that has not been prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2)(c).  (2) The regulations may, for the purposes of subsection (1), prescribe that:  (a) the cost of a particular material, or a part of such a cost; or  (b) a particular labour cost, or a part of a labour cost; or  (c) a particular overhead cost, or a part of an overhead cost; is not allowable in respect of goods, or classes of goods.  (3) The regulations may, for the purposes of subsection (1), prescribe the manner of working out:  (a) the cost of a material, or part of the cost; or  (b) a labour cost, or part of the cost; or  (c) an overhead cost, or part of the cost. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The cost of producing or manufacturing goods is worked out, for the purposes of section 255, by adding up the following amounts:  (a) the amount of expenditure on materials in respect of the goods;  (b) the amount of expenditure on labour in respect of the goods;  (c) the amount of expenditure on overheads in respect of the goods; each worked out in accordance with this table:  Cost of producing or manufacturing goods Item This amount of expenditure: is worked out as follows: Expenditure on materials in respect of the goods The cost of materials used in the production or manufacture of the goods: (a) that is incurred by the manufacturer of the goods; and (b) that has not been prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2)(a). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 Cost of producing or manufacturing goods Item This amount of expenditure: is worked out as follows: Expenditure on labour in respect of the goods The sum of each labour cost: (a) that is incurred by the manufacturer of the goods; and (b) that relates to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (c) that can reasonably be allocated to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (d) that has not been prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2)(b). Expenditure on overheads in respect of the goods The sum of each overhead cost: (a) that is incurred by the manufacturer of the goods; and (b) that relates to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (c) that can reasonably be allocated to the production or manufacture of the goods; and (d) that has not been prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2)(c).  (2) The regulations may, for the purposes of subsection (1), prescribe that:  (a) the cost of a particular material, or a part of such a cost; or  (b) a particular labour cost, or a part of a labour cost; or  (c) a particul"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e11603014f3ad2f41fb6bb39a4ee793422dabc453a7a8a321333fa178248cf14" ;
