concept:act-sch-2-sec-263-2-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "263(4) Consequences of rejecting goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-263-2-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The supplier must, in accordance with an election made by the consumer:  (a) refund:  (i) any money paid by the consumer for the goods; and  (ii) an amount that is equal to the value of any other consideration provided by the consumer for the goods; or  (b) replace the rejected goods with goods of the same type, and of similar value, if such goods are reasonably available to the supplier." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The supplier must, in accordance with an election made by the consumer:  (a) refund:  (i) any money paid by the consumer for the goods; and  (ii) an amount that is equal to the value of any other consideration provided by the consumer for the goods; or  (b) replace the rejected goods with goods of the same type, and of similar value, if such goods are reasonably available to the supplier."@en ;
