concept:act-sch-2-sec-263-2-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "263(6) Consequences of rejecting goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-263-2-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If the property in the rejected goods had passed to the consumer before the rejection was notified, the property in those goods revests in the supplier on the notification of the rejection. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If the property in the rejected goods had passed to the consumer before the rejection was notified, the property in those goods revests in the supplier on the notification of the rejection. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "88f10df644be76e2daa2b17ee047217f2671430b381e152785d269237573b829" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-263-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "248"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Property reverts to supplier upon notification of rejection." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
