    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the failure to comply with the guarantee can be remedied and is not a major failure:  (a) the consumer may require the supplier to remedy the failure within a reasonable time; or  (b) if such a requirement is made of the supplier but the supplier refuses or fails to comply with the requirement, or fails to comply with the requirement within a reasonable time—the consumer may:  (i) otherwise have the failure remedied and, by action against the supplier, recover all reasonable costs ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 incurred by the consumer in having the failure so remedied; or  (ii) terminate the contract for the supply of the services." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the failure to comply with the guarantee can be remedied and is not a major failure:  (a) the consumer may require the supplier to remedy the failure within a reasonable time; or  (b) if such a requirement is made of the supplier but the supplier refuses or fails to comply with the requirement, or fails to comply with the requirement within a reasonable time—the consumer may:  (i) otherwise have the failure remedied and, by action against the supplier, recover all reasonable costs ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 incurred by the consumer in having the failure so remedied; or  (ii) terminate the contract for the supply of the services."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9d67ff4c9c7769e423ab47b71665fcee3d6762e88456f187df904f9628c5451c" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "250"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Supplier must remedy failure within a reasonable time or face termination of contract." ;
    dc:description "Remediation and costs incurred by consumer" ;
