concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5 cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-1 .
concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-1 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "implies" ;
    cml:logicSummary "If conditions are met, then it is an obligation." ;
    cml:premiseText "The services would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure." ;
    cml:conclusionText "It is an obligation to comply with the guarantee." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5 cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2 .
concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:AllenInterval ;
    cml:operator "during" ;
    cml:logicSummary "The conditions describe a temporal relationship between the failure and the acquisition of services." ;
    cml:premiseText "Both (i) and (ii) apply: the services, and any product resulting from the services, are unfit for a particular purpose for which the services were acquired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier of the services; the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The failure occurred during the acquisition of services." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::interval_reasoning" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5 cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-ltl-3 .
concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-ltl-3 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:LTL ;
    cml:operator "everywhere" ;
    cml:logicSummary "The conditions describe a universal property of major failures." ;
    cml:premiseText "A failure to comply with a guarantee is a major failure if certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Major failures have the same properties as specified in the conditions." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::temporal_ltl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5 cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-4 .
concept:act-sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "entails" ;
    cml:logicSummary "The conditions imply that it is an obligation to comply with the guarantee." ;
    cml:premiseText "A failure to comply with a guarantee is a major failure if certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:conclusionText "It is an obligation to comply with the guarantee." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-267-2-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "267(5) Action against suppliers of services" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) To avoid doubt, subsection (4) applies in addition to subsections (2) and (3). 268  When a failure to comply with a guarantee is a major failure  A failure to comply with a guarantee referred to in section 267(1)(b) that applies to a supply of services is a major failure if:  (a) the services would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the nature and extent of the failure; or  (b) the services are substantially unfit for a purpose for which services of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or  (c) both of the following apply:  (i) the services, and any product resulting from the services, are unfit for a particular purpose for which the services were acquired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier of the services;  (ii) the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to make them fit for such a purpose; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    cof:pageNumber "250"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-246-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "246 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-246-3 ;
    values:originalText "(d) both of the following apply:  (i) the services, and any product resulting from the services, are not of such a nature, or quality, state or condition, that they might reasonably be expected to achieve a result desired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier;  (ii) the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to achieve such a result; or  (e) the supply of the services creates an unsafe situation." ;
    skos:definition "(d) both of the following apply:  (i) the services, and any product resulting from the services, are not of such a nature, or quality, state or condition, that they might reasonably be expected to achieve a result desired by the consumer that was made known to the supplier;  (ii) the services, and any of those products, cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be remedied to achieve such a result; or  (e) the supply of the services creates an unsafe situation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f3f6ca717e8e704e59d95dd3ba1426f145f57bc699f9297ad902778dca1741ef" ;
    cof:pageNumber "252"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Services and products must be of a certain nature, quality, state or condition to achieve a desired result by the consumer." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.252" ;
