concept:act-sch-2-sec-258-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "258 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-258-3 ;
    values:originalText "(ii) such other matters as appear to be relevant in the circumstances of the case.  (5) The matter for the purposes of subsection (4) is that the linked credit provider, before first becoming aware of:  (a) the contract of sale referred to in paragraph (a) of that subsection; or  (b) proposals for the making of such a contract; had not had cause to suspect that a person entering into such a contract with the supplier might be entitled to claim damages against, or recover a sum of money from, the supplier for a misrepresentation, breach, failure of consideration, failure to comply with a guarantee, or a breach of a warranty, referred to in section 278(1).  (6) This section has effect despite section 278(1)." ;
    skos:definition "(ii) such other matters as appear to be relevant in the circumstances of the case.  (5) The matter for the purposes of subsection (4) is that the linked credit provider, before first becoming aware of:  (a) the contract of sale referred to in paragraph (a) of that subsection; or  (b) proposals for the making of such a contract; had not had cause to suspect that a person entering into such a contract with the supplier might be entitled to claim damages against, or recover a sum of money from, the supplier for a misrepresentation, breach, failure of consideration, failure to comply with a guarantee, or a breach of a warranty, referred to in section 278(1).  (6) This section has effect despite section 278(1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5e36d56f1716ee336429e643327346c0322e147b6dbc5ae0eaf5b74c9924cd4f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "264"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-258-3-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-258-3-ss-6 ;
