concept:act-sch-2-sec-283-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "283 Enforcement of judgments etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-283-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If, in joint liability proceedings, judgment is given against a supplier and a linked credit provider, the judgment must not be enforced against the credit provider unless a written demand made on the supplier for satisfaction of the judgment has remained unsatisfied for at least 30 days.  (2) If the judgment can be enforced against the linked credit provider, it may only be enforced to the extent of the lesser of the following amounts:  (a) the amount calculated in accordance with section 281;  (b) so much of the judgment debt as has not been satisfied by the supplier.  (3) If, in joint liability proceedings, a right conferred by section 282(3) is established by a consumer against a linked credit provider, the consumer must not receive the benefit of the right unless:  (a) judgment has been given against the supplier and credit provider; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If, in joint liability proceedings, judgment is given against a supplier and a linked credit provider, the judgment must not be enforced against the credit provider unless a written demand made on the supplier for satisfaction of the judgment has remained unsatisfied for at least 30 days.  (2) If the judgment can be enforced against the linked credit provider, it may only be enforced to the extent of the lesser of the following amounts:  (a) the amount calculated in accordance with section 281;  (b) so much of the judgment debt as has not been satisfied by the supplier.  (3) If, in joint liability proceedings, a right conferred by section 282(3) is established by a consumer against a linked credit provider, the consumer must not receive the benefit of the right unless:  (a) judgment has been given against the supplier and credit provider; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "22ad26a48ba538f676dd340a83baf5b238de90e8a3d9dfd537cad2533c3d9d8b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "265"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-283-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-283-2-ss-2 ;
