    cml:conclusionText "...to ensure that no inconsistency arises between..." ;
    cml:executionSurface "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-131c-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "131C(2) Saving of other laws and remedies" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Section 73 of the Australian Consumer Law does not operate in a State or a Territory to the extent necessary to ensure that no inconsistency arises between:  (a) that section; and  (b) a provision of a law of the State or Territory that would, but for this subsection, be inconsistent with that section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "275"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-131c-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "131C(3) Saving of other laws and remedies"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-131c-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Despite subsection (1):  (a) if an act or omission of a person is both:  (i) an offence against this Part or the Australian Consumer Law; and  (ii) an offence against a law of a State or a Territory; and  (b) the person is convicted of either of those offences; he or she is not liable to be convicted of the other of those offences." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Despite subsection (1):  (a) if an act or omission of a person is both:  (i) an offence against this Part or the Australian Consumer Law; and  (ii) an offence against a law of a State or a Territory; and  (b) the person is convicted of either of those offences; he or she is not liable to be convicted of the other of those offences."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "531309b1ca33f21e735debee65830ffafc620ba8a0ae8340b0c8db6fb3bee243" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-131c ;
    cof:pageNumber "275"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemptions from concurrent prosecution for offenses against multiple laws." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
