concept:act-sch-2-sec-272-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-272-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The proposed ban notice must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be published on the internet; and  (c) set out a copy of a draft notice for the imposition of the interim ban or permanent ban; and  (d) set out a summary of the reasons for the proposed imposition of the ban; and  (e) invite any person who supplies, or proposes to supply:  (i) consumer goods of that kind; or  (ii) product related services of that kind;  to notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified in the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a conference in relation to the proposed imposition of the ban.  (4) The period specified in the proposed ban notice under paragraph (3)(e):  (a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as the Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and  (b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is published.  (5) A proposed ban notice is not a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The proposed ban notice must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be published on the internet; and  (c) set out a copy of a draft notice for the imposition of the interim ban or permanent ban; and  (d) set out a summary of the reasons for the proposed imposition of the ban; and  (e) invite any person who supplies, or proposes to supply:  (i) consumer goods of that kind; or  (ii) product related services of that kind;  to notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified in the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a conference in relation to the proposed imposition of the ban.  (4) The period specified in the proposed ban notice under paragraph (3)(e):  (a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as the Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and  (b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is published.  (5) A proposed ban notice is not a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a14d25efc6fbfea8c191603579f9d001281ec4e72cd7d7a905baaad63c1eda9a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-272-3-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-272-3-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-272-3-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.278" .
doc:sch-2-sec-272-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "272 Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The proposed ban notice must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be published on the internet; and  (c) set out a copy of a draft notice for the imposition of the interim ban or permanent ban; and  (d) set out a summary of the reasons for the proposed imposition of the ban; and  (e) invite any person who supplies, or proposes to supply:  (i) consumer goods of that kind; or  (ii) product related services of that kind;  to notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified in the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a conference in relation to the proposed imposition of the ban.  (4) The period specified in the proposed ban notice under paragraph (3)(e):  (a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as the Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and  (b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is published.  (5) A proposed ban notice is not a legislative instrument." ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer .

