doc:sch-2-sec-132a-2-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "132A(3) Commonwealth Minister must issue a proposed recall notice" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The proposed recall notice must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be published on the internet; and  (c) set out a copy of a draft recall notice; and  (d) set out a summary of the reasons for the proposed issue of the recall notice; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (e) invite any person who supplies, or proposes to supply, consumer goods of that kind to notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified in the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a conference in relation to the proposed issue of the recall notice." ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-132a-2-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "132A(4) Commonwealth Minister must issue a proposed recall notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-132a-2-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The period specified in the proposed recall notice under paragraph (3)(e):  (a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as the Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and  (b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is published." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The period specified in the proposed recall notice under paragraph (3)(e):  (a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as the Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and  (b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is published."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "79509e9ce6134c605020d5066011a72309811ac5481e1c4aadcf0a66ec176fa2" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-132a-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minimum period for proposed recall notice" ;
    dc:description "10 days or longer" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
