    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If one or more persons notify the Commission in accordance with a notice published under subsection 132E(2) that they wish the Commission to hold a conference, the Commission must:  (a) appoint a day, time and place for the holding of the conference; and  (b) give written notice to the Commonwealth Minister, and to each person who so notified the Commission, of that day, time and place. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law" ;
