concept:act-sch-2-sec-133f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133F Compliance with disclosure notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-133f ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is given a disclosure notice; and  (b) the person refuses or fails to comply with the notice. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person complies with the disclosure notice to the extent to which the person is capable of complying with the notice. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. 133G  False or misleading information etc.  A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in purported compliance with a disclosure notice; and  (b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or document is false or misleading in a material particular. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is given a disclosure notice; and  (b) the person refuses or fails to comply with the notice. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person complies with the disclosure notice to the extent to which the person is capable of complying with the notice. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. 133G  False or misleading information etc.  A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in purported compliance with a disclosure notice; and  (b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or document is false or misleading in a material particular. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0ae64da3e22c3b4f32dd23072030f1970e8fdf23f2f8051919f90aba68553a33" ;
    cof:pageNumber "289"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-133f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-133f-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-133f-ss-3 ;
