    skos:definition "(1) If a court is satisfied that:  (a) a person possesses or has control of consumer goods of a particular kind; and  (b) any of the following apply:  (i) the consumer goods do not comply with a safety standard that is in force for consumer goods of that kind and the cause of that non-compliance cannot be remedied;  (ii) a permanent ban on consumer goods of that kind is in force;  (iii) a recall notice for consumer goods of that kind is in force and a defect or dangerous characteristic of such consumer goods identified in the notice cannot be remedied; the court may, on the application of an inspector, make an order of a kind referred to in subsection (2)."@en ;
