concept:act-sch-2-sec-133h-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133H(2) Court orders relating to consumer goods that do not comply"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-133h-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The court may make an order under subsection (1) authorising one or more inspectors to do the following in accordance with any requirements specified in the order:  (a) to enter the premises of the person that are specified in the order;  (b) to search the premises for consumer goods of a kind specified in the order;  (c) to seize any such consumer goods that are found at those premises;  (d) to destroy or otherwise dispose of any such consumer goods that are so seized. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The court may make an order under subsection (1) authorising one or more inspectors to do the following in accordance with any requirements specified in the order:  (a) to enter the premises of the person that are specified in the order;  (b) to search the premises for consumer goods of a kind specified in the order;  (c) to seize any such consumer goods that are found at those premises;  (d) to destroy or otherwise dispose of any such consumer goods that are so seized. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "61c58bae56f1f6ab49dc21660f7c18c03b1cff0c7e2641b725565a0b5e523325" ;
