concept:act-sch-2-sec-133j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133J Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing, and destroying or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-133j ;
    values:originalText "disposing of, consumer goods  (1) If an inspector seizes, and destroys or otherwise disposes of, consumer goods in accordance with an order made under subsection 133H(1):  (a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized; or  (b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods— the owner of the consumer goods; is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in seizing, and in destroying or disposing of, the consumer goods.  (2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction." ;
    skos:definition "disposing of, consumer goods  (1) If an inspector seizes, and destroys or otherwise disposes of, consumer goods in accordance with an order made under subsection 133H(1):  (a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized; or  (b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods— the owner of the consumer goods; is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in seizing, and in destroying or disposing of, the consumer goods.  (2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0d5874930d9cb3dc52eddedde94f482ae50230c66225e474bcd317edd6962abe" ;
    cof:pageNumber "291"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-133j-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-133j-ss-2 ;
