concept:act-sch-2-sec-135c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135C Failure to answer questions or produce documents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-135c ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection 135B(2); and  (b) the person fails to comply with the requirement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—150 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—30 penalty units.  (2) A person is not excused from:  (a) answering a question; or  (b) producing a document; as required under subsection 135B(2) on the ground that the answer, or production of the document, might tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection 135B(2); and  (b) the person fails to comply with the requirement. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—150 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—30 penalty units.  (2) A person is not excused from:  (a) answering a question; or  (b) producing a document; as required under subsection 135B(2) on the ground that the answer, or production of the document, might tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "028aaa39230b3457c41b34944bad7d73fbb0684d939140257598771e38a9d995" ;
    cof:pageNumber "303"^^xsd:integer ;
