concept:act-sch-2-sec-135d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135D Persons assisting inspectors"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-135d ;
    values:originalText "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons  (1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in exercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be assisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and reasonable.  (2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector. Powers of a person assisting the inspector  (3) A person assisting the inspector may:  (a) enter the premises; and  (b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but only in accordance with a direction given to the person by the inspector.  (4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned in subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by the inspector. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    skos:definition "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons  (1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in exercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be assisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and reasonable.  (2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector. Powers of a person assisting the inspector  (3) A person assisting the inspector may:  (a) enter the premises; and  (b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but only in accordance with a direction given to the person by the inspector.  (4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned in subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by the inspector. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66856edc540bc7beff27d40f88dfc0bb58ad5f467677634e23c89876ed9b16db" ;
    cof:pageNumber "304"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135d-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135d-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135d-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.304" .
doc:sch-2-sec-135d a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "135D Persons assisting inspectors" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons  (1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in exercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be assisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and reasonable.  (2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector. Powers of a person assisting the inspector  (3) A person assisting the inspector may:  (a) enter the premises; and  (b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but only in accordance with a direction given to the person by the inspector.  (4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned in subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by the inspector. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010" ;
    cof:pageNumber "304"^^xsd:integer .

