doc:sch-2-sec-135j a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "135J Details of search warrant etc. must be given to the occupier of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the premises  If:  (a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises; and  (b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who apparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises; an inspector executing the warrant must, as soon as practicable:  (c) do one of the following:  (i) if the warrant was issued under section 135Z—make a copy of the warrant available to the occupier or other person (which need not include the signature of the judge who issued it);  (ii) if the warrant was signed under section 136—make a copy of the form of warrant completed under subsection 136(7) available to the occupier or other person; and  (d) inform the occupier or other person of the rights and responsibilities of the occupier or other person under Subdivision C. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010 Subdivision C—Occupier’s etc. rights and responsibilities" ;
    cof:pageNumber "306"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-135k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135K Occupier etc. entitled to observe execution of search warrant"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-135k ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises; and  (b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who apparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises; the occupier or other person is entitled to observe the execution of the warrant.  (2) The right to observe the execution of the search warrant ceases if the occupier or other person impedes that execution.  (3) This section does not prevent the execution of the search warrant in 2 or more areas of the premises at the same time." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises; and  (b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who apparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises; the occupier or other person is entitled to observe the execution of the warrant.  (2) The right to observe the execution of the search warrant ceases if the occupier or other person impedes that execution.  (3) This section does not prevent the execution of the search warrant in 2 or more areas of the premises at the same time."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "77934fbb2a7a15a9ea7a556bc0e889f013f28a5dfd4ab7c383fd4c5e2141773c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "307"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135k-ss-2 ;
