concept:act-sch-2-sec-135y a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135Y Compliance with embargo notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-135y ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person, contrary to the embargo notice, does an act or omits to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person causes another person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (i) to do an act that is contrary to the embargo notice; or  (ii) contrary to the embargo notice, to omit to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (1) or (2) does not apply in relation to:  (a) an act done in accordance with a consent given under section 135X; or  (b) if the embargo notice relates to consumer goods—an act done for the purpose of protecting or preserving the consumer goods; or  (c) if the embargo notice relates to product related services—an act done for the purpose of protecting or preserving equipment used to supply the services. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.  (4) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(b) and (2)(b). Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. Subdivision F—Issue of search warrants" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person, contrary to the embargo notice, does an act or omits to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person causes another person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (i) to do an act that is contrary to the embargo notice; or  (ii) contrary to the embargo notice, to omit to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (1) or (2) does not apply in relation to:  (a) an act done in accordance with a consent given under section 135X; or  (b) if the embargo notice relates to consumer goods—an act done for the purpose of protecting or preserving the consumer goods; or  (c) if the embargo notice relates to product related services—an act done for the purpose of protecting or preserving equipment used to supply the services. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.  (4) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(b) and (2)(b). Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. Subdivision F—Issue of search warrants"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b6f87f50d7feb84c05e931b67750ee8894499017838a9c651d0d34b31f344bcc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "314"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135y-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135y-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135y-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-135y-ss-4 ;
