    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person, contrary to the embargo notice, does an act or omits to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "314"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-2-sec-135y-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135Y(2) Compliance with embargo notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-135y-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person causes another person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (i) to do an act that is contrary to the embargo notice; or  (ii) contrary to the embargo notice, to omit to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person causes another person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (i) to do an act that is contrary to the embargo notice; or  (ii) contrary to the embargo notice, to omit to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f429e92611c971e1518be5fd27ac2f9e64c503980f86b9c0476fd4a7a9bd4b84" ;
