    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person knows that an embargo notice has been given; and  (b) the person causes another person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2) 2010  (i) to do an act that is contrary to the embargo notice; or  (ii) contrary to the embargo notice, to omit to do an act. Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units." ;
