concept:act-sch-2-sec-136b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "136B Powers of judges"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-136b ;
    values:originalText "Powers conferred personally  (1) A power conferred on a judge by this Division is conferred on the judge:  (a) in a personal capacity; and  (b) not as a court or a member of a court. Powers need not be accepted  (2) The judge need not accept the power conferred. Protection and immunity  (3) A judge exercising a power conferred by this Division has the same protection and immunity as if he or she were exercising the power:  (a) as the court of which the judge is a member; or  (b) as a member of the court of which the judge is a member." ;
    skos:definition "Powers conferred personally  (1) A power conferred on a judge by this Division is conferred on the judge:  (a) in a personal capacity; and  (b) not as a court or a member of a court. Powers need not be accepted  (2) The judge need not accept the power conferred. Protection and immunity  (3) A judge exercising a power conferred by this Division has the same protection and immunity as if he or she were exercising the power:  (a) as the court of which the judge is a member; or  (b) as a member of the court of which the judge is a member."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a3d9ce38f203e8b183955c1df3c707be225fa24ea2ebd96628bb6f45dc1fcae0" ;
