concept:act-sch-2-sec-138c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "138C Transfer of matters by the Federal Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-138c ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), if:  (a) a civil proceeding instituted by a person (other than the Commonwealth Minister or the Commission) is pending in the Federal Court; and  (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law; the Federal Court may, on the application of a party to the proceeding or of its own motion, transfer the matter, and any other matter for determination in the proceeding, to a court of a State or a Territory. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), if:  (a) a civil proceeding instituted by a person (other than the Commonwealth Minister or the Commission) is pending in the Federal Court; and  (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law; the Federal Court may, on the application of a party to the proceeding or of its own motion, transfer the matter, and any other matter for determination in the proceeding, to a court of a State or a Territory. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1b7b67d67f8dda24d70f4a2f24960de7080c49f7587d1e159000b5abf784f874" ;
    cof:pageNumber "329"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Transfer of matters by the Federal Court" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.329" ;
    cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-138c-norm .
