    values:originalText "(2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes of paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a consumer contract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the Commonwealth Minister must take into consideration:  (a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to consumers; and  (b) the impact on business generally of prescribing that kind of term or effect; and  (c) the public interest." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes of paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a consumer contract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the Commonwealth Minister must take into consideration:  (a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to consumers; and  (b) the impact on business generally of prescribing that kind of term or effect; and  (c) the public interest."@en ;
