    skos:prefLabel "140F(2) How duty is imposed"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-140f-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The duty is taken not to be imposed by this Act (or any other law of the Commonwealth) to the extent to which:  (a) imposing the duty is within the legislative powers of the State or Territory concerned; and  (b) imposing the duty by the law of the State or Territory is consistent with the constitutional doctrines restricting the duties that may be imposed on the entity. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The duty is taken not to be imposed by this Act (or any other law of the Commonwealth) to the extent to which:  (a) imposing the duty is within the legislative powers of the State or Territory concerned; and  (b) imposing the duty by the law of the State or Territory is consistent with the constitutional doctrines restricting the duties that may be imposed on the entity. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 2  Application of the Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
