doc:sch-4-sec-356-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "356(7) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (1), a court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  (a) which persons are non-parties in relation to the contravening conduct;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. When a non-party is bound by an order etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "362"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-4-sec-356-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "356(8) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-356-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) If:  (a) an order is made under subsection (1) against a person; and  (b) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by a non-party in relation to the contravening conduct to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (c) the non-party has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction; then:  (d) the non-party is bound by the order; and  (e) any other order made under subsection (1) that relates to that loss or damage has no effect in relation to the non-party; and  (f) despite any other provision of this Act or any other law of the Commonwealth, or a State or Territory, no claim, action or demand may be made or taken against the person by the non-party in relation to that loss or damage. 51ADC  Kinds of orders that may be made to redress loss or damage suffered by non-parties etc.  Without limiting subsection 51ADB(1), the orders that a court may make under that subsection against a person (the respondent) include all or any of the following:  (a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a contract made between the respondent and a non-party referred to in that subsection, or a collateral arrangement relating to such a contract: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 4  Enforcement of industry codes" ;
    skos:definition "(8) If:  (a) an order is made under subsection (1) against a person; and  (b) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by a non-party in relation to the contravening conduct to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (c) the non-party has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction; then:  (d) the non-party is bound by the order; and  (e) any other order made under subsection (1) that relates to that loss or damage has no effect in relation to the non-party; and  (f) despite any other provision of this Act or any other law of the Commonwealth, or a State or Territory, no claim, action or demand may be made or taken against the person by the non-party in relation to that loss or damage. 51ADC  Kinds of orders that may be made to redress loss or damage suffered by non-parties etc.  Without limiting subsection 51ADB(1), the orders that a court may make under that subsection against a person (the respondent) include all or any of the following:  (a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a contract made between the respondent and a non-party referred to in that subsection, or a collateral arrangement relating to such a contract: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00868  Schedule 4  Enforcement of industry codes"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0f5c32c749f2dd82408b04e0d77d1abea091b957d58ea5789f0ec15650dd694c" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-4-sec-356 ;
    cof:pageNumber "362"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Non-party bound by order if loss or damage is redressed, prevented, or reduced." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
